This is the initial version of the CHANGES file for the project. It outlines the changes made in each version of the software, providing a clear history of updates, bug fixes, and new features.

# 0.9.0-RC3

- addressed all the outstanding known security issues

- rebrended everything to OpenServerless, removing all the references to the original source

- images has been updated for compliance with ASF rules. Most notably psycopg has been removed and replacds with pg8000, and incompatbile biaries (most notably mc) has been removed

- entirely rewritten the entire build system, documented in BUILD.md - governed by triggering by tags and manually

- now there is one python:sys image for executing system actions, the preloader preloads the images also from non-apache sources and preload the python:sys image

# 0.9.0-RC4

- bun.lockb -> bun.lock (text)

- excluded binary files (almost all test data and the gradle-wrappers from openwhisk)

- backported SSO from 0.9.1 branch

# 0.9.0-RC5

- changed dependencies of python runtimes for license incompatibilites
- cleaned all the .licenserc and added a top level rat- reworked all the LICENSE and NOTICE files
- reworked the cli to use license headers
- cleaned some leftover olaris -> oplugins

# 0.9.0-RC6

- cleaned LICENSES and NOTICE including embedded packages and deployment descriptors
- certmanager is now downloaded on demand with helm
- removed minio and all the utils, renamed as generic s3
- removed mongodb support entirely (monngodb name retained meaning ferretdb)
- fixed issues in the ops setup server deployment
- added tika support

# 0.9.0-RC7
- moved oplugins/util/config to its own openserverless-configurator repo
- do no not add OPS_BRANCH in ~/.profile any more
- updated the LICENSE and NOTICE for oplugins and top level

# 0.9.0 (Unreleased)

- Require FerretDB client credentials and correct tenant database/role provisioning and cleanup.
- Restrict CouchDB user metadata access to administrators.
- Restrict Redis tenant command, key and channel permissions while preserving tenant-scoped Lua; persist tenant ACLs on persistent volumes across Redis restarts.
- Forward termination signals to Redis so graceful shutdown can save pending RDB writes.
- Scope anonymous S3 reads to declared public web buckets; reconcile and verify restored IAM before resuming ingress.
- Add NetworkPolicies and internal Services limiting tenant action access to etcd, Milvus management, Kafka, ZooKeeper, SeaweedFS control APIs and shared monitoring (requires an enforcing CNI); reduce monitoring Secret access and reconcile its RBAC during operator updates.
- Generate installation-specific etcd JWT signing keys, scope Milvus access to etcd, store Milvus configuration in Secrets and redact configuration values from debug logs.
- Enforce authentication before executing custom OPTIONS handlers on protected web actions, preserving automatic CORS preflight handling.
- Require OIDC issuer/subject ownership before issuing tenant credentials; add a separate Secret-authorized tenant provisioning API and install its scoped RBAC during K3s setup.
- Validate runtime-build image references and tenant ownership; isolate rootless BuildKit jobs with user namespaces, no service-account token and process sandboxing.
- Isolate malformed Cron annotations between tenants and bound cron-init jobs, HTTP requests and paginated scans while retaining Allow concurrency. Duplicate prevention and recovery of missed executions remain separate work.
- Wait for API ingress, registry credentials and default-tenant readiness during full cluster setup; validate component dependencies before reporting success.
- Update the default K3s installation to v1.36.4+k3s1 and Milvus to v2.5.27; align the image catalog and correct the devcontainer image tag.
- Fix operator image build ownership and provide a valid default Alertmanager receiver when notifications are disabled.
- Restore valid TOML comments in uv.lock so the Admin API can start.
- Prevent operator image publication on branch pushes, including branch names containing slashes.
- Strengthen operator integration regression gates, use private service endpoints in SeaweedFS tests, and correct FerretDB and static-content assertions; propagate setup and HTTP failures.
- Preserve bundled JavaScript license texts, correct NOTICE attribution and document/exclude generated OpenWhisk checkouts and overlay archives from source distributions.
- Add an SSO configuration guide covering provider examples, login flows, provisioning defaults, rollout and troubleshooting.
